From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: quiesce wifili offload at SERVER_EXIT before WCSS reset

A Wi-Fi firmware assert drives the ahb SSR path through
ath11k_core_pre_reconfigure_recovery(), which stops the mac80211 queues and
drains host TX but leaves the NSS wifili firmware armed and still driving the
WCSS HAL SRNG pointer registers. Those registers are held in reset while the Q6
reboots, so the NSS core takes an external abort and coredumps - and because
wifili and the wired data path share NSS core0, the coredump brings the whole
box down and the recovery re-arm re-trips it into a reboot loop.

Send the wifili STOP message at SERVER_EXIT, before the WCSS reset lands, so the
NSS firmware ceases touching the reset register space. The full teardown in
ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() still runs its stop/deinit/reset and ignores
this stop's return, so no dynamic-interface node leaks and the offload re-arms
cleanly once the Q6 is back.

Guard the stop on wifili actually being registered. Cold-boot calibration
restarts the Q6 through ath11k_core_pre_reconfigure_recovery() on every
normal boot, before ath11k_nss_init_soc() runs, when ab->nss.if_num is
still 0; nss_wifili_tx_msg() then rejects the message as a non-wifili
interface and the stop fails with NSS_TX_FAILURE. ab->nss.ctx is set only
by init_soc and never cleared, so it distinguishes "never started" from
"started" without affecting the assert path this patch exists for.

The guard sits in ath11k_nss_stop() rather than in the new caller, so all
three stop paths share it. The other two cannot currently reach it with a
null ctx - ath11k_nss_teardown() is only called after a successful setup
or from behind ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, and the setup error path runs after
init_soc - but the precondition belongs with the message that requires it.
Guarding ath11k_nss_teardown() as a whole would instead skip its pdev
deinit, reset and tx descriptor free.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index a1d76bc..48f14dd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2532,6 +2532,8 @@
 
 	wake_up(&ab->wmi_ab.tx_credits_wq);
 
+	ath11k_nss_pre_reconfigure(ab);
+
 	reinit_completion(&ab->driver_recovery);
 }
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -3417,6 +3417,13 @@
 	nss_tx_status_t status;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* Cold-boot calibration restarts the Q6 through pre_reconfigure before
+	 * ath11k_nss_init_soc() has registered wifili, when if_num is still 0
+	 * and the message is rejected as a non-wifili interface.
+	 */
+	if (!ab->nss.ctx)
+		return 0;
+
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_NSS, "NSS stop\n");
 	wlmsg = kzalloc(sizeof(struct nss_wifili_msg), GFP_ATOMIC);
 	if (!wlmsg)
@@ -3554,6 +3561,14 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+int ath11k_nss_pre_reconfigure(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+{
+	if (!ab->nss.enabled)
+		return 0;
+
+	return ath11k_nss_stop(ab);
+}
+
 int ath11k_nss_setup(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 {
 	int i;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.h
@@ -280,6 +280,7 @@
 				  struct hal_rx_user_status *user_stats);
 int ath11k_nss_setup(struct ath11k_base *ab);
 int ath11k_nss_teardown(struct ath11k_base *ab);
+int ath11k_nss_pre_reconfigure(struct ath11k_base *ab);
 void ath11k_nss_ext_rx_stats(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct htt_rx_ring_tlv_filter *tlv_filter);
 #else
 static inline int ath11k_nss_tx(struct ath11k_vif *arvif, struct sk_buff *skb)
@@ -447,6 +448,11 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static inline int ath11k_nss_pre_reconfigure(struct ath11k_base *ab)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static inline void ath11k_nss_ext_rx_stats(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 					   struct htt_rx_ring_tlv_filter *tlv_filter)
 {
